{
  "about": "A Date column's values (ADR-0023, ADR-0350 section 16): a date and time compared by its fields, a day by its day, an instant by the instant it names; every cell and operand held to the column's declared date type. {\"dateTime\": text} is a DateTime in C# and a Temporal.PlainDateTime in the Script Core, {\"dateOnly\": text} a DateOnly and a Temporal.PlainDate, {\"dateTimeOffset\": text} a DateTimeOffset and a Temporal.ZonedDateTime at that offset, {\"jsDate\": text} a DateTimeOffset and a JavaScript Date. From dotnet/tests/ExGrid.Tests/SortSemanticsTests.cs, DateOperatorTests.cs, DateTimeOffsetSemanticsTests.cs and DeclaredDateTypeTests.cs.",
  "kind": "query",
  "columns": [{"name": "Book", "type": "text"}, {"name": "TradedOn", "type": "date", "dateType": "dateTime"}, {"name": "Settles", "type": "date", "dateType": "dateOnly"}, {"name": "Stamped", "type": "date", "dateType": "dateTimeOffset"}],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "ADR-0023: dates and times sort chronologically, Blanks last when descending too",
